<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8cc54168235ceeaf561c7e77c0b661ed053bcd4b" commit="766d60d7008e7b2e35271381b6019dd11b9bdc6d" commit_message="drivers/flash: Support mmaped flash with non-zero base offset  In some boards e.g. reef, the entire flash is not memory mapped. Instead only a part of the flash (offset 0x1000 to offset x which covers the BIOS region) is mapped in the address space. In order to handle such special cases, a new API is required to allow boards to define the offset on flash of the base address that is memory mapped. This base offset needs to be taken care of while accessing any absolute address within the mmaped range. For older boards, this base_offset defaults to 0.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54563 BRANCH=None TEST=Compiles successfully and boots to OS on reef.  Change-Id: I8cc54168235ceeaf561c7e77c0b661ed053bcd4b Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354380 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354380" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/80/354380/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If928c3af762adfe6752ba55e39f995309f195c79" commit="9df74f5da895200d036dd2811281e8a8c7ac1b9e" commit_message="reef: Calculate BIOS mmap details at runtime  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54563 BRANCH=None TEST=Compiles successfully and boots to OS on reef.  Change-Id: If928c3af762adfe6752ba55e39f995309f195c79 Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354381 Commit-Ready: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354381" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/81/354381/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iad09914d79cdbd798fb650146321eafed06eb91c" commit="9c94575008683bea87a7515954fa80e37c4090c1" commit_message="reef: Enable external power interrupt GPIO  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54503 BRANCH=none TEST=Manually tested using console commands on both the ports.      a. Issued 'gpioget AC_PRESENT', observed AC_PRESENT is         1 when AC connected &amp; 0 when AC disconnected.      b. Issued 'hibernate' &amp; on plugging in the AC, device         boots to S0.  Change-Id: Iad09914d79cdbd798fb650146321eafed06eb91c Signed-off-by: Vijay Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354721 Commit-Ready: Vijay P Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Tested-by: Vijay P Hiremath &lt;vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354721" owner_email="vijay.p.hiremath@intel.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/21/354721/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I08036ff6614482a529d1d404a63cbdcc405db1a3" commit="6eba138f23c8afa275176c817b495ede24d41934" commit_message="metrics: create a more convenient wrapper around ts_mon  ts_mon has some unfriendly eccentricities: 1) it may fail to import, and we don't want to handle that in every calling module. 2) it needs special handling when re-fetching a handle for a given metrics from the same process  This CL creates a more friendly handler around ts_mon, which makes it safe in all cases to do:  import metrics  metrics.Counter('foo').increment()  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I08036ff6614482a529d1d404a63cbdcc405db1a3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354691 Commit-Ready: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Aviv Keshet &lt;akeshet@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354691" owner_email="akeshet@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/91/354691/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic91f34b60b11ebce948bce01993ddb44519a59b8" commit="2965fe00978ada6b5d80eb574219b57540827c5a" commit_message="bdb: Add vba_update_buc  vba_update_buc writes a BUC (boot unlock code) to NVM-RW. It will be called by AP-RW to update a BUC.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:51907 BRANCH=tot TEST=make runtests  Change-Id: Ic91f34b60b11ebce948bce01993ddb44519a59b8 Signed-off-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346233 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346233" owner_email="dnojiri@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/33/346233/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6cc7ddf36bb7fa9762627a8b1a2ed34db27206b4" commit="3bbca02bbecca8b0f3b78d2a400bfb1566b05683" commit_message="mariadb: work around cros copmiliation error.  New cmake_utils.eclass detects the build of mariadb on the guado-moblab board is cros build. It disables the build of some binary that runs on the host, this causes the build failure. This CL workarounds it by letting cros compiler build binary that runs on the host. This is the old/working behavior.  BUG=chromium:621558 TEST=ebuild-guado-moblab mariadb passes on upstream cmake-utils.eclass  Change-Id: I6cc7ddf36bb7fa9762627a8b1a2ed34db27206b4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354692 Commit-Ready: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354692" owner_email="yunlian@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/92/354692/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ib17052cf004b3f5a3eaad3553af06e4ea87abbd2" commit="515b9d73c6dc0d70ad8654d326efe03f399ec556" commit_message="CHROMIUM: ASoC: ipq4019: dma_resume only when dma started  MBOX DMA resume is meaningful only in the following situations:  1. DMA is started; MBOX engine has exhausted the queued descriptors;     and has gone into a STALLED state since there are no more     descriptors for it to process.    (or)  2. DMA is active  When DMA is resumed in state '1', MBOX resumes fetching and processing the descriptors. And, in state '2', the resume is ignored.  Initiating a DMA resume when the MBOX is not in one of the above states can potentially confuse the MBOX state machine causing it to refetch previous descriptors and play them resulting in static/random noise. Hence, added a flag to track if the MBOX is already started before resuming the DMA.  [This is a rework of https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/353515 .  Kudos to Balamurugan Selvarajan &lt;bselvara@codeaurora.org&gt; for debugging  and proposing the initial fix.]  BUG=chrome-os-partner:53767 TEST=unit tested audio driver with below test cases.        1. Tested for static noise during playback        2. Tested for noise during the start/end of the audio        3. Loop audio playback for 500 times. Should play without           random noise, crash or hangs.  Change-Id: Ib17052cf004b3f5a3eaad3553af06e4ea87abbd2 Signed-off-by: Grant Grundler &lt;grundler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354084 Tested-by: Balamurugan Selvarajan &lt;bselvara@codeaurora.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Balamurugan Selvarajan &lt;bselvara@codeaurora.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354084" owner_email="grundler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/84/354084/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I2b87be5395d6ddcaa76265879feb2097889f0a01" commit="2309d902da8833ab37f2d43d987c801fff474bca" commit_message="CHROMIUM: cros_ec: Set driver names properly.  Use cros-ec-&lt;function&gt; driver name convention, regardless of the driver file name. Use MODULE_ALIAS when only one type of platform device is exposed by the driver.  BUG=chromium:617704 TEST=check on chell cros-ec-usbpd-charger as a module is loaded properly.  Change-Id: I2b87be5395d6ddcaa76265879feb2097889f0a01 Signed-off-by: Gwendal Grignou &lt;gwendal@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/354777 Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="354777" owner_email="gwendal@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/77/354777/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1b7b25903c20788e8487ab5ebb3ec7c51470fd76" commit="aa522630c265058065b2ccf0c42d7a7124bd8e6b" commit_message="tpm: move buffer size definition to common code  Also change it to match the naming pattern o